From: INMYS <support@inmys.ru>
Subject: [PATCH] spi: silvaco: clear the QSPI1 pad open-drain bit

The HSPERIPH URB resets the QSPI1 pad configuration register (offset
0x1c) to 0x7, i.e. pad enable | 1.8 V | **open drain**.  U-Boot's
mcom03_qspi_set_soc_regs() only touches the enable and the 1.8 V bits,
so the pads stay in open-drain mode: the controller can pull the lines
low but has to rely on pull-ups for the high level.

That is enough for a single-byte command with an all-zero address --
`sf probe 1:0` happily reports

	SF: Detected w25q80ew with page size 256 Bytes, erase size 4 KiB, total 1 MiB

-- but every real transfer comes back as 0xbb, and because 0xbb is
uniform the whole chip even has a plausible-looking CRC.  Erasing a
sector and reading it back still returns 0xbb, which is what gave the
game away.

QSPI is a push-pull bus, so clear the open-drain bit together with the
enable.  After that the same W25Q80EW reads back a blank 1 MiB
(crc32 956bac74) and erase/write/verify work.

Signed-off-by: INMYS <support@inmys.ru>
---
diff -urN a/drivers/spi/silvaco_qspi.c b/drivers/spi/silvaco_qspi.c
--- a/drivers/spi/silvaco_qspi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/silvaco_qspi.c
@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@
 #define QSPI1_PAD		0x1c
 #define QSPI1_PAD_EN		1
 #define QSPI1_PAD_1V8		BIT(1)
+#define QSPI1_PAD_OPEN_DRAIN	BIT(2)
 
 #define QSPI1_SS		0x20
 #define QSPI1_SISO		0x24
@@ -135,7 +136,17 @@
 		debug("\nHint: QSPI1 pads are configured as %s\n", is_18v ?
 		      "1.8V" : "3.3V");
 
-		ret = regmap_update_bits(regmap, QSPI1_PAD, QSPI1_PAD_EN, QSPI1_PAD_EN);
+		/*
+		 * The pads come out of reset with the open-drain bit set, so
+		 * the controller can only pull the lines low and relies on
+		 * pull-ups for the high level.  A single-byte command such as
+		 * READ ID survives that, but any real transfer does not: on a
+		 * W25Q80EW in the ELV-SMARC-CB socket every data byte reads
+		 * back as 0xbb.  QSPI is a push-pull bus, clear the bit.
+		 */
+		ret = regmap_update_bits(regmap, QSPI1_PAD,
+					 QSPI1_PAD_EN | QSPI1_PAD_OPEN_DRAIN,
+					 QSPI1_PAD_EN);
 		if (ret < 0)
 			return ret;
 
